c41174a9 (2762 1793916818449 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f428") (src . "split-suggest: shell and Perl files are read line by line\n\nA language entry may carry line-suggest beside its lexical profile.\nWhen suggest-boundaries is called without starts (split-suggest with\nno symbols file, and a file's first cut into blocks on import) and the\nentry has it, the file is read line by line: a definition is a line\nthat matches one of the entry's definition heads at column 0, the\ncomment run above it goes with it, and no bracket, quote or heredoc is\nfollowed, so nothing is lexically uncertain and a head inside a\nheredoc is taken as written. The routes that are given starts, the\nchecked symbols import and split-suggest with symbols, never see it.\n\nThe shell entry gains an empty line-suggest and keeps its brace\nprofile for the checked routes. A new Perl entry (pl, pm, t) has sub\nand package heads, an identifier that spells a qualified name as one\ntoken, no lexical profile, and stop lines: a line that is exactly\n__END__ or __DATA__ ends the reading, that line and the rest staying\nin the last block. Symbols given for a Perl file are unchecked.\n\nA line is decoded by one function for every scan, which keeps a\nbyte-order mark inside the file as the character it is instead of\nraising; and an unbalanced closer is reported at its byte offset, the\ntext before it on its line counted in bytes.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 641))))
